{%- doc -%}
  Loading placeholder for the contact band. Figma "Contact us skeleton"
  7930:94604.

  Used by both pages this band appears on - the contact page (7930:94717) and
  About (7930:95474) - so it traces the band, not the page.

  Figma's skeleton also shows a large hero tile above the cards. Neither page
  has an image there, so reproducing it would promise something that never
  arrives and jump the layout when the cover lifts. The heading, subcopy and
  three cards are what this actually resolves to.

  See assets/skeleton.css for how this clears.

  @param {number} [cards] - cards in the row, to match the section's blocks
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign card_count = cards | default: 3
  if card_count < 1
    assign card_count = 1
  endif
-%}

<div class="contact-skeleton skeleton" data-skeleton aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="contact-skeleton_wrapper">
    <span class="skeleton_tile" style="height: 34px; width: 280px"></span>
    <span class="skeleton_tile" style="height: 22px; width: 58%"></span>

    <div class="contact-skeleton_wrapper_cards">
      {%- for card in (1..card_count) -%}
        <span class="skeleton_tile skeleton_tile--card contact-skeleton_wrapper_cards_item"></span>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
